## What I built

**Concept — the line of energy.** A movement is one push handed along six times, so the page is organised around a single hairline that starts under the hero, becomes the charged spine of the power path, becomes the edge of the layer stack, rules the spec ledger, and ends at the reservation. Colour is sampled from the movement photography: German-silver paper, gilt brass, the ruby of a jewelled bearing, graphite.

**Sections, in order:** hero (dark, photographic) → the beat claim with a marker ticking at the movement's real 2.5 Hz → **the power path** (peak) → the four-layer stack → specification → the workshop → three finishes + reservation → footer.

**Signature component:** the power path. Six stages on a line whose charge fills from one authored scroll-progress value; the reached station lights, the sticky index on the left shows position and lets you jump to any stage, and the escapement/balance stages run the 2.5 Hz beat. Second: the layer stack drawn as an edge-on elevation at true relative thickness — 0.9 + 1.4 + 0.8 + 0.7 visibly adds up to the 3.8 mm on the spec sheet — with hover/click/arrow-key separation.

**State propagation:** choosing or hovering a finish lights that finish's share of the 200-movement allocation mark in the workshop section, and fills the reservation summary and confirmation.

**Media:** three CC BY-SA 2.0 macro photographs of mechanical movements by GuySie (Flickr, via Openverse), graded and used as material grounds — credited in the footer and in `public/media/CREDITS.md`, and explicitly not presented as photographs of Caliber 08. The schematic diagrams are drawn, which is the right medium for a cutaway; no fabricated product photography.

**Preserved:** all six stages in order with detail and figure, four layers with thicknesses and notes, all ten spec rows, three finishes with exact CHF prices/dates/remaining, all five workshop facts including the run of 200 and the indefinite servicing commitment, the form, and the non-binding/no-payment statement (on both the form and the confirmation).

## Verified in the browser

Desktop 1440, 390 and 320 px: no horizontal overflow, no console or page errors. Reservation flow exercised end to end at both widths — confirmation reads *"…we have held one Open-worked movement at CHF 39'500 … Delivered from September 2027."* Keyboard: skip link, focus rings, arrow-key layer selection, radio-group focus. Reduced motion renders every section fully with the beat static. One correction cycle is in `shots/` (the power path originally had a half-empty sticky column and pale stage rows; it was rebuilt as sticky index + charged line with right-aligned figures).

Two notes: I left the `shots/` directory in the working tree — delete it if you don't want it. And the CC BY-SA licence on the photography is share-alike, which the footer credit satisfies but which you'd want to confirm suits a real commercial page.

Implementation complete; human taste verdict: awaiting user review — please look at `shots/desktop.png`, `shots/mobile.png`, and the power path mid-scroll (`shots/d-path-300.png`).